00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Autumn Sonata (Swedish: Höstsonaten) is a 1978 tragedy film written and directed by Ingmar Bergman,
and starring Ingrid Bergman (in her final film role), Liv Ullmann and Lena Nyman.

11
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:36,000
Its plot follows a celebrated classical pianist and her neglected daughter who meet for the first time
in years, and chronicles their painful discussions of how they have hurt each other.

12
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
It was the only collaboration between Ingrid Bergman and
Ingmar Bergman (who were not related).

13
01:11:30,000 --> 01:11:36,000
Autumn Sonata was the last of Ingmar Bergman's films to be made for theatrical exhibition; all of his
films made after it, even those screened in theatres, were television productions.

14
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:06,000
The film explores themes of violin, sonata, creepy house.

15
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
